# What lives here, and why none of it is committed.
#
# harvis.crt / harvis.key — the certificate and its private key. A private key
#   must never reach a repository, and a certificate is only valid for the
#   machine and addresses it was generated for.
#
# harvis-tls.conf — the activated HTTPS listener. If a clone shipped this
#   without the certificate it points at, nginx would refuse to start and take
#   the whole front door down on a fresh install. Only the .template is tracked;
#   scripts/enable-https.sh makes the copy locally.
#
# The directory itself IS tracked (via this file and the .template), which is
# what guarantees it exists in a fresh clone — an absent bind-mount source is
# created by Docker as root, and the setup script could not write into it.
harvis-tls.conf
*.crt
*.key
*.pem
*.csr
*.redirect
